  "skill_description": "Use for Azure access and identity workflows: Entra API JWT validation and record ownership, browser/session PKCE and Container Apps frontend sign-in, native Easy Auth/MSAL, managed identity and Bicep/AVM, PIM and deployment approvals, RBAC and Cosmos/ADX/SQL/Graph permissions, 401/403 diagnosis, exact-scope verification and owned cleanup. Native administrative procedures only; installed entra_auth and signed_dev_access own auth mechanisms. Plans never execute commands or grant authority; cloud mutations need explicit target-bound authorization. Replaces the former separate entra-api-auth, entra-auth-container-apps and bicep-managed-identity entries; no azaccess engine or MCP runtime.",
  "skill_body": "# Azure Access And Identity\n\nRead the [canonical guide](../../../libraries/entra-auth/docs/skills/azure-access-management.md)\nand [native administrative procedures](../../../libraries/entra-auth/docs/skills/native-access-workflows.md).\nUse installed `entra-auth` (`entra_auth`) for strict token/PKCE/store mechanisms\nand canonical `signed_dev_access` for request signatures. Hosts own authorization,\nsessions and deployment. `azaccess`, legacy auth helpers and MCP runtimes are\nretired; this entry grants no credentials, inference, role or resource mutation.",
